{"title":"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(exponent_rules)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (exponent rules)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1b956218eae738b1fb5f2e55874afa82ca8a48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{3} = 8^{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f4c59777e0869603ba433076902552c1298f40d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\sqrt{3} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"403\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1b956218eae738b1fb5f2e55874afa82ca8a48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{3} = 8^{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/33225e104124ff3710208835d861ee73564aa104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{a} = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>This is true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b4a6d33ecb561cf3e697a339099ced26cd16c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"91\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28exponent_rules.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(exponent_rules)\">Solution 2 (exponent rules)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (exponent rules)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are both powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, we can make the bases both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> using exponent rules:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc05b0f13ea619f073e035f6e19636f5ab9178ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^{2})^{3} = (2^{3})^{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf0f287125a0a6422880a4b94afae62009899daa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2 \\times 3} = 2^{3 \\times a} = 2^{a \\times 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Because the bases are equal to each other, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/1120d72b8c2505c002e92f54ee4ceb2155db428c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3 = a \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. We can clearly see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b4a6d33ecb561cf3e697a339099ced26cd16c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"91\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(answer_choices)\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and both are positive integers, we can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b689abbbf1e231f489d17f9fd1ec5a19e9fe61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8c4ea7b36568bfe5163b6cf852deb837198a8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> would be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b453a3053437d48e460262328c419c415f64329d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />. This eliminates all answer choices except A and B.\n</p><p>We also realize that A cannot be the answer because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b453a3053437d48e460262328c419c415f64329d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> must be an integer, and we don't get an integer value for the right hand side of the equation if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> were to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. This eliminates answer choice A.\n</p><p>Because all of the other answer choices are eliminated, we can see that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b4a6d33ecb561cf3e697a339099ced26cd16c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"91\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2025 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> 